  "cli_result_text": "Submitted 17 files spanning both repos that map the customer's regression:\n\n**Babel side** \u2014 decision point and ordering:\n- `babel-plugin-proposal-decorators/src/index.ts` \u2014 chooses legacy (stage-2) vs createClassFeaturePlugin (stage-3) based on `.legacy`/`.version`\n- `babel-plugin-proposal-decorators/src/transformer-legacy.ts` \u2014 legacy-form transform (what Nest.js requires)\n- `babel-helper-create-class-features-plugin/src/decorators.ts` \u2014 stage-3 implementation (does *not* emit `Reflect.metadata`)\n- `babel-plugin-syntax-decorators/src/index.ts` \u2014 validates/normalizes the `legacy`/`version` options\n- `babel-preset-typescript/src/index.ts` + `babel-plugin-transform-typescript/src/index.ts` \u2014 TS strip that must run after decorators are handled; plugins run before presets in Babel's ordering\n- READMEs confirm Babel core has no built-in `emitDecoratorMetadata`/`Reflect.metadata` equivalent\n\n**SWC side** \u2014 parallel path and divergence:\n- `crates/swc/src/config/mod.rs` \u2014 defines `jsc.transform.legacyDecorator` and `jsc.transform.decoratorMetadata` (both default `false`)\n- `crates/swc_ecma_transforms_proposal/src/decorators/mod.rs` \u2014 dispatches to `legacy::new(emit_metadata)` vs the stage-3 `Decorators` fold based on `Config.legacy`\n- `crates/swc_ecma_transforms_proposal/src/decorators/legacy/mod.rs` + `.../legacy/metadata.rs` \u2014 the legacy `__decorate`/`__metadata` emission, explicitly ported from `babel-plugin-transform-typescript-metadata` (confirming Babel itself never had this natively)\n- `crates/swc_ecma_transforms_proposal/src/decorator_2022_03.rs` \u2014 stage-3 TC39 form (no metadata support \u2014 SWC's own `unimplemented!()` guard fires if you combine `emit_metadata` with non-legacy)\n- `crates/swc/src/builder.rs` + `crates/swc/src/lib.rs` \u2014 pass ordering guarantee (\"decorators, then resolver, then TS strip\" runs before any custom pass)\n- `crates/swc_ecma_transforms_typescript/src/lib.rs` \u2014 confirms TS strip itself contains no decorator logic; it's a separate pass\n\nThe divergence: the customer's SWC config almost certainly has `legacyDecorator: true` but is missing `decoratorMetadata: true` (both default `false`), so `@injectable()` still fires as a legacy decorator but no `design:paramtypes`/`Reflect.metadata` call is ever emitted \u2014 DI resolution then reads undefined metadata.",
